====================================================================
                        AbstractSet
====================================================================

AbstractSet: Is a base class providing common functionality for Set implementations.
             It is a generic class that requires its elements to implement the Comparable<E>
             interface. It also implements the SetADT<E> interface.
             It provides shared functionality such as tracking the number of elements (private int count),
             checking whether the set is empty (boolean isEmpty()), returning the set size (int size()),
             and clearing the set (void clear()). Concrete subclasses are responsible for implementing
             the element specific operations, such as add(), remove(), contains(), and iterator().

Attribute
----------------------------------------------
    - **count - int : Attribute that track how many element the Set contains.


Method
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    - **AbstractSet() - No-type : No-argument constructor that initializes the [count] attribute to zero.
    - **remove(E element) - boolean : Abstract method that removes the specified element from the set if it is present.
    - **contains(E element) - boolean : Abstract method that checks whether the specified element exists in the set.
    - **contains(E element) - boolean : Abstract method that checks whether the specified element exists in the set.
    - **size() - int : Method that returns the number of elements in the set.
    - **isEmpty() - boolean : Method that checks whether the set contains no elements.
    - **clear() - void : Method that removes all elements from the set by resetting the [count] attribute.
    - **iterator() - Iterator<E> : Abstract method that returns an iterator over the elements in the set.
